From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilMetaMonkey <hood.mj85@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:17:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/31] Make hooks uninstall restore the original config bytes

Uninstall now drops a "hooks" object it emptied, deletes a config file
left empty (one dmc created), and writes in the original file's layout
(single-line or its indent, and its final newline). Before, uninstalling
from Muse Code's settings.json left "hooks": {} and a trailing newline,
and a created .claude/settings.local.json was left as {"hooks": {}}.

Muse Code scope notes now reflect the 1.4.13 probe: project hooks run
only in a trusted workspace, so user settings stay the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/src/hook_installer.dart   | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 test/hook_installer_test.dart | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/src/hook_installer.dart b/lib/src/hook_installer.dart
